    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0745" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">417.41/–</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1916-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1252</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of Your Excellency’s note of the 29th ultimo, enclosing four lists of
                    claims against Nicaragua for consideration in connection with the distribution
                    of the amount to be paid to Nicaragua in accordance with the recent Treaty with
                    that country.</p>
                <p>The Department regrets that it cannot, at the present time, outline any plan for
                    the distribution of the amount to be paid to Nicaragua pending the actual
                    appropriation and an arrangement with the Republic looking to that end.</p>
                <p>The claims submitted will, however, receive the Department’s careful
                    consideration along with many other similar ones now on file.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
